THOUGHT: The NullAway error is because `path` is annotated `@Nullable` in `getFileName(@Nullable URL path)` but is dereferenced without a null check. The simplest fix is to handle the null case explicitly, returning an empty string (consistent with the `String` overload’s behavior for invalid inputs). I’ll update that method accordingly and then run the build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '110,112c\  public static String getFileName(@Nullable URL path) {
    if (path == null) {
      return "";
    }
    return getFileName(path.getPath());
  }' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/util/io/FileUtilities.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -i "NullAway" -n new_build_output.log | tail -n 5
```

